    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n96758" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στία</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῑ], ἡ</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>small stone, pebble</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐσχάρη . . στιάων</span> an altar made of
			<i>pebbles</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				2.1172
			</span></i> (Sicyonian acc. to Sch.): also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στῖον</span></b> , τό, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				19.140
			</span></i>. [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῑ</span>: written
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στηά</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στηάς</span> in <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, who adds the senses <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στενοχωρία</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λιθοκονία</span>: pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεῖαι</span>
			acc. to Sch.Cyrill.in <i><span class="en">Reitzenstein
					<u>Ind.Lect.Rost.</u>1890</span></i>/<i><span class="en">
				91.8
			</span></i>: perh. cogn. with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στέαρ</span>.]</div>
